WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.700
Here's what these two gates
prove, against NIST's catalog.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.763
Vulnerabilities by software
and update support

3
00:00:06.763 --> 00:00:09.825
vulnerability monitoring
and flaw remediation.

4
00:00:09.825 --> 00:00:14.713
Every exposed device owned, or a finding,
supports the component inventory.

5
00:00:14.713 --> 00:00:17.460
The Exposure Management
disposition supports

6
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.138
vulnerability monitoring,
honestly recorded.

7
00:00:20.138 --> 00:00:24.285
Incidents owned inside their windows
and closed with a classification

8
00:00:24.285 --> 00:00:28.087
support incident handling, incident
monitoring, and audit review.

9
00:00:28.087 --> 00:00:31.899
And the incident record with its alerts
supports the reporting decision.

10
00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:35.088
The indicators are FedRAMP's,
as the guide maps them.

11
00:00:35.088 --> 00:00:38.950
The records support these controls;
the assessor decides them.
